                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Fantastic. I decided to pick this game up while looking for cryptid hunting games.\r\n\r\nIt turned out to be exactly what I wanted/expected (at least for the first part) a slow-ish paced exploration/walking-sim game. Although, the second part of the game leans more towards fps.\r\n\r\nThe open world non-linearity is executed very well, so that the game does not restrict you but still offers enough guidance to get you on the right path. No hand holding works great! Though I did struggle while searching for a specific item and only realized later that I had missed it in a very obvious spot... (the axe).\r\n\r\nAs for the story... I'm not sure David Lynch would be very impressed, but as a regular player I kind of enjoyed it. It does keep you hooked!\r\n\r\nHighly recommend, especially on sale.",
